# Locus of Enlightenment: "Whenever you activate an ability that isn't a mana ability, copy it." The copy is made even if
# the ability was countered before the trigger resolves: it is copied as it last was on the stack (CR 707.10, 608.2h; the
# Rings of Brighthearth ruling, "they resolve even if that ability is countered"). Bot1 crafts Locus on turn 7 as in the
# crafting scenario and activates the Goblin Bombardment ability it has, sacrificing an Ornithopter, at Bot2. With Locus's
# trigger on the stack Bot2 flashes in Ertai Resurrected, whose trigger counters the original ability (Bot1, its
# controller, draws a card). The trigger then copies it, keeping Bot2 as the target: Bot2 takes 1, from the copy alone.

